; status: works — axiom 4: project a corner onto a slanted line, crease ⊥ another line
; .c is folded onto --l1 moving along the direction of --l2; the crease ends up
; perpendicular to --l2. Render folded (`fold2svg --folded`) to watch the corner
; land on --l1; render the crease pattern to see the crease sit perpendicular to --l2.
paper square
; scaffold: two midlines give the non-corner points .tm and .rm
mark --vmid = map .a onto .b              ; x = 1/2
mark --hmid = map .a onto .d              ; y = 1/2
.tm = --vmid * --cd                  ; midpoint of the top edge,   (1/2, 1)
.rm = --hmid * --bc                  ; midpoint of the right edge, (1, 1/2)
; two generic slanted lines — slopes 1/2 and 2, neither a diagonal
mark --l1 = through .a .rm                ; the line .c lands on
mark --l2 = through .a .tm                ; the crease is forced perpendicular to this
; fold corner .c onto --l1, crease perpendicular to --l2
fold map .c onto --l1 perp --l2 moving .c

; `faces` is the evaluator's crease-pattern state: the one fold subdivides
; to 2; --vmid/--hmid/--l1/--l2 stay unfolded marks there (they graduate to
; F creases, adding more faces, only in the emitted FOLD)
; assert faces = 2
; assert steps = 1
; assert .c = (2/3, 1/3)
